GITM-RT segment input, rendered by rt/segment.py from rt/templates/UAM.in.rt.
Physics choices follow srcData/UAM.in (the maintained default).

#DEBUG
0		debug level (0 = no info, 10 = max info)
0		cpu to watch
60.0		dt between normal code output to stdout
F		usebarriers - forces the code to stop and wait more often

#RESTART
${RESTART}		Restart Code

start time is only honored on cold starts; restarts take time from restartIN

#TIMESTART
${START_YEAR}		year
${START_MONTH}		month
${START_DAY}		day
${START_HOUR}		hour
${START_MINUTE}		minute
${START_SECOND}		second

#TIMEEND
${END_YEAR}		year
${END_MONTH}		month
${END_DAY}		day
${END_HOUR}		hour
${END_MINUTE}		minute
${END_SECOND}		second

#GRID
${NBLK_LON}		number of blocks in longitude
${NBLK_LAT}		number of blocks in latitude
-90.0		minimum latitude to model
90.0		maximum latitude to model
0.0		longitude start to model (set to 0.0 for whole Earth)
0.0             longitude end to model (set to 0.0 for whole Earth)

DtRestart is large on purpose: the clean-exit restart written by finalize is
the segment checkpoint; mid-segment restart writes are not wanted.

#SAVEPLOTS
${DT_RESTART}		dt for writing restart files
1		how many output files do you want
3DALL		output style
${DT_PLOT}		dt for output

#ELECTRODYNAMICS
${AURORAL_MODEL}
60.0
weimer05
60.0

${DRIVER_LINES}

#DYNAMO
T		UseDynamo
45.0		DynamoHighLatBoundary
500		nItersMax
1.0		MaxResidual
F		IncludeCowling
40.0		LongitudinalAveraging
F               UseNewTrace

#APEX
T

#MSISOBC
T		Shift the [O] density at the lower boundary by 6 months
0.0		change the obateness of the Earth by this percent (0 = none)

#AUSMSOLVER
T       	Use AUSM+-up Solvers

#END
